{"id":"0ce064881a79d6f7","group":"89","path":"89/89-df-arithmetical-soundness.md","title":"Arithmetical Soundness","display":"df-arithmetical-soundness — Arithmetical Soundness","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-df-arithmetical-soundness","aliases":["89-df-arithmetical-soundness"],"display":"df-arithmetical-soundness — Arithmetical Soundness","depends_on":["[[89-df-provable-formula]]","[[89-df-peano-arithmetic]]","[[89-df-arithmetical-semantics]]"],"created":"2026-10-05","revised":"2026-10-09"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-df-arithmetical-soundness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-df-arithmetical-soundness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-arithmetical-soundness — Arithmetical Soundness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2d52ad4f119b4a14\" href=\"?note=2d52ad4f119b4a14\" title=\"89-df-provable-formula\">89-df-provable-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"86ad48bbd1843ed6\" href=\"?note=86ad48bbd1843ed6\" title=\"89-df-peano-arithmetic\">89-df-peano-arithmetic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8811191242063297\" href=\"?note=8811191242063297\" title=\"89-df-arithmetical-semantics\">89-df-arithmetical-semantics</a></span></div>"},{"key":"created","html":"2026-10-05"},{"key":"revised","html":"2026-10-09"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_{\\mathrm{PA}}\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_{\\mathrm{PA}}\\)</span>，标准结构 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb N=(\\mathbb N,0,S,+,\\times)\">\\(\\mathbb N=(\\mathbb N,0,S,+,\\times)\\)</span> 取通常运算。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb N\\models A\">\\(\\mathbb N\\models A\\)</span> 是元语言的递归一阶满足关系，不是 PA 中的全局真谓词。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProvFml}(T)\">\\(\\mathrm{ProvFml}(T)\\)</span> 是元层可证句子集；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ArSound}(T)\">\\(\\mathrm{ArSound}(T)\\)</span> 是下述定义的标准模型可靠性谓词。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProvFml}(T)\">\\(\\mathrm{ProvFml}(T)\\)</span> 使用对任意公理集给出的演算定义；本谓词没有隐含的递归可枚举性前提。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}arithmetical\\text{-}soundness}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ArSound}(T)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\forall A\\in\\mathrm{ProvFml}(T)\\ (\\mathbb N\\models A).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}arithmetical\\text{-}soundness}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ArSound}(T)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\forall A\\in\\mathrm{ProvFml}(T)\\ (\\mathbb N\\models A).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Boolos, <em>The Logic of Provability</em>，第 3 章，印刷页 62–65；PDF 页码为印刷页加 39。本条采用本目录的等价语法约定。\n这比仅不证明矛盾的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Cons}(T)\">\\(\\mathrm{Cons}(T)\\)</span> 强。PA 的公理及经典推理在标准结构中保真，故通常元理论下 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ArSound}(\\mathrm{PA})\">\\(\\mathrm{ArSound}(\\mathrm{PA})\\)</span> 成立。Solovay 的原书证明在第 9 章确实用到“PA 所证都真”，以下采用这一来源支持的条件；不把它声称为所有算术完备性版本的最弱假设。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"89-df-provable-formula","status":"resolved","id":"2d52ad4f119b4a14","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-provable-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"